Add the NativeDwc3 built-in personality. Like NativeUfs's root personality, it
matches the platform-expert (root) device so the probe can start early, before the
original AMFI. It is unconditional: a personality is a runtime string resolved by
class name, so when the NativeDwc3 archive is not linked (any board that does not
force_load libNativeDwc3.a) IOKit simply finds no such class and does not match.
On enchilada the archive is linked (CONFIG_XNU_EXTRA_LD_ARCHIVES); the driver is still
default-off, doing nothing unless the boot argument native-dwc3-probe=1 is set.

Anchored on the IOExclaveProxy entry, which no other patch in the series touches, and
inserted before that entry rather than after it.  The build re-runs every patch on the
second pass and leaves alone any patch whose reverse check still applies, so a patch
must not sit inside another patch's context: native-aes-personality.patch ends its
guards just before the table's closing parenthesis, and armvirt-platform-personality.patch
ends just before the IOPanicPlatform entry, so this board's block goes between them.
diff --git a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
--- a/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
+++ b/iokit/KernelConfigTables.cpp
@@ -42,3 +42,9 @@
+    "   {"
+    "     'IOClass'         = NativeDwc3;"
+    "     'IOMatchCategory' = NativeDwc3;"
+    "     'IOProviderClass' = IOPlatformExpertDevice;"
+    "     'IOProbeScore'    = 400:32;"
+    "   },"
     "   {"
     "     'IOClass'         = IOExclaveProxy;"
     "     'IOProviderClass' = IOService;"
